menu "NEON LINK — Neon Sync"

config NEON_SYNC
    bool "Use Neon Sync (Link-free session protocol) instead of Ableton Link"
    default n
    depends on !NEON_LINK_STUB
    help
        Replaces the Ableton Link session with Neon Sync, our own
        leaderless session protocol (docs/NEON_SYNC.md): same
        hal::ILinkSession seam, same downstream behavior, no GPL
        dependency in the image. Peers discover each other over UDP
        multicast (239.77.83.78:20809), agree on tempo/phase/transport
        last-writer-wins, and discipline clocks via NTP-style ping/pong —
        or via the AP's TSF beacon clock when two peers share a BSS.

        Neon Sync peers do not interoperate with Ableton Link peers on
        the wire; Live is bridged via MIDI clock or the VST3 plugin.

endmenu
